  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Firebase Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now diving into the Firebase skill guidelines, specifically the `/skills/system_skills/firebase-skill/SKILL.md` document. My current focus is on the requirements, specifically the need for a `firebase-blueprint.json` file. This blueprint is crucial as it defines the schema for our Firestore collections, so I\'m studying this file.\n\n\n**Analyzing Firestore Design**\n\nI\'m now thinking about the Firestore data structure. I\'m focusing on the `firestore.rules` file for security. Also I am thinking about `/src/lib/firebase.ts` (or `/src/firebase.ts`), and how it initializes firebase. I\'ve got to design the schema based on the user\'s calorie-tracking requirements. This includes recording daily calories, user limits, BMR/TDEE calculations, macronutrient tracking, and a saved foods list. I\'m making sure to address the calorie details: consumption, remaining calories to BMR, and TDEE.\n\n\n**Developing User Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating several UI components. I\'m building a weight-tracking interface with an input for daily weight and implementing a Recharts line chart to visualize weight trends. I am adding a water intake tracker with a cup counter, adjustable cup capacity, and daily goal setting with animations. Furthermore, I\'m working on Google Sign-In via `GoogleAuthProvider` and Firebase authentication, including guest mode and fallback for iframe scenarios. I\'ll be storing user data in Firestore by their `userId`. I\'m starting on the first version of the dashboard.\n\n\n**Designing Dashboard View**\n\nI\'m now deep in thought about the dashboard view. I envision a comprehensive summary with progress rings and gauges for calories, BMR, TDEE, and macronutrients. I\'m planning pie/bar charts for macronutrient distribution and a visual water progress tracker, alongside a weight trend preview. The quick food add form will be included. I\'m structuring a multi-tab navigation system, including dashboard, food log, weight trend, water tracker, food library, and settings/profile.\n\n\n**Defining User Profile Fields**\n\nI\'m now focusing on user profile details within the `firebase-blueprint.json` schema. I\'m defining fields like gender, age, height, weight, activity level, BMR, TDEE, custom calorie targets, and water intake settings, including cup volume and daily goals. These are all critical to personalize calculations, and they are required elements in the profile.\n\n\n**Structuring Food Log Schema**\n\nI\'m now deep into designing the data schema for the food log in `firebase-blueprint.json`. I\'m meticulously defining each field: `date`, `mealType`, `foodName`, `calories`, macronutrients (`proteinGrams`, `carbsGrams`, `fatGrams`, `fiberGrams`), serving details, and `createdAt`. I\'m paying careful attention to data types and descriptions, and determining the required fields to ensure data integrity, especially `userId`, `date`, `foodName` and `calories`. Furthermore, I am designing the `weightLogs` collection with its properties and requirements.\n\n\n**Defining Water Log Schema**\n\nI\'m now building the `waterLogs` schema for `firebase-blueprint.json`, with the required fields: `userId`, `date`, and `cups`. I\'m also including `cupVolumeMl`, `totalMl`, and `updatedAt`. I\'m ensuring data types and descriptions are correct to ensure data integrity.\n\n\n**Implementing Security Rules**\n\nI am now structuring the `firestore.rules` file for security, focusing on access control based on user authentication and ownership. I\'m implementing helper functions for authentication and checking ownership with the appropriate rules. I am ensuring that the `users` and top level collections, like `userProfiles` and `foodLogs`, are correctly secured. I\'m focusing on allowing read and write access to authenticated users only, while restricting access to documents based on user ID matching the authenticated user\'s ID.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 12
      nanos: 518461523
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
