    thinking: "**Constructing the Dashboard**\n\nI\'m now focusing on building the `Dashboard.tsx` component. I\'ve begun analyzing the requirements, starting with the need for a Calorie Target Card. This card will display today\'s total consumed calories alongside the daily BMR target, expressed in kcal. My current thought process centers around the best way to represent this information clearly and concisely.\n\n\n**Designing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now sketching out the dashboard visuals. I\'ve decided on \"\350\267\235\351\233\242\345\237\272\347\244\216\344\273\243\350\254\235\347\216\207 (BMR) \351\202\204\345\267\256 XXX kcal\" as the BMR indicator. I\'ll add \"\350\267\235\351\233\242\347\206\261\351\207\217\344\270\212\351\231\220 (TDEE) \351\202\204\346\234\211 XXX kcal\" or \"\345\267\262\350\266\205\345\207\272\344\270\212\351\231\220 XXX kcal!\" for the TDEE limit, paired with a progress bar for both BMR and TDEE. I\'m prioritizing clarity and using visual cues to show progress towards goals. Next, I\'m conceptualizing the macronutrient breakdown display.\n\n\n"
